.claude/settings.local.json
.DS_Store

# gophics CLI build output
/build/

# Go test binaries. `go test -c` and a failed `go test -o` drop these in the
# package directory; they are ~20MB each and the per-name list below cannot
# anticipate them.
*.test
*.test.exe

examples/build/

# Example web/app build artifacts
examples/*/web/*.wasm
examples/*/web/wasm_exec.js

# Android build trees (any example)
examples/*/android/app/libs/*.aar
examples/*/android/.gradle/
examples/*/android/app/build/
examples/*/android/local.properties

# iOS build trees (any example)
examples/*/ios/build/
examples/*/ios/build-sim/

# Generated docs-site artifacts (rebuilt by .github/workflows/pages.yml)
docs/demos/
docs/source/

# Stray example binaries from `go build ./examples/<x>` without -o.
# One entry per example (regenerate with: ls examples/ | grep -v build).
# CI's tracked-binary guard catches any that slip through.
# Compiled example binaries. `go build ./examples/<name>` drops an
# extensionless binary here named after the example, and this list is
# maintained by hand — so every new example is unignored until someone
# remembers to add a line. That is how a 19MB luminaria binary reached the
# index; the pre-push size gate is what caught it.
/luminaria
/mirror
/telemetry
/2048
/canvas
/drummachine
/epub
/flocking
/flowfield
/gallery
/glass
/gpucheck
/health
/hello
/hn
/journal
/ledger
/match3
/mover
/notes
/particles
/roguelike
/solitaire
/ssh
/sudoku
/todo
/whiteboard

# `go build ./examples/<name>` drops the binary in the repo root by default.
# Several slipped into commits at ~18 MB each; the compiled examples are build
# output. The named entries above cover the ones that did.
/counter

# gomobile bind output. These were tracked and reached ~200 MB across their
# versions before being purged from history; package/ios.sh regenerates them.
examples/*/ios/*.xcframework/

# Debug image dumps, written by the gg tests "for visual inspection" and read by
# nothing. 41 of them were tracked, so every `go test ./...` left 41 modified
# files in the working tree — a first contribution starts with a dirty diff, and
# a real change to a golden becomes invisible in the noise.
#
# The comment here used to say the tracked ones were golden references. They
# were not: the suite passes with the whole directory deleted and recreates all
# 62 files. The actual goldens are in internal/gfx/gg/testdata/golden/, loaded
# by loadGoldenPNG — read rather than written, which is the difference.
internal/gfx/gg/tmp/

# Ad-hoc measurement harnesses built into the repo root. These are named after
# whatever they were probing, so the per-example list below cannot anticipate
# them — cpudmg and webdmg were built to measure present-path bytes and reached
# a commit at 19MB each, together with a stale `gophics` CLI build.
/cpudmg
/webdmg
/gophics

# Binaries from a separate-module example, which are named after the module
# rather than the directory and so are missed by the per-example list above.
# `go build ./...` inside examples/ssh or examples/embed-ebiten drops one; both
# reached the index that way, at 19 MB and 27 MB.
examples/*/gophics-*
